__pycache__/
*.pyc

# app/app.yaml IS TRACKED AS OF  and must not be ignored. The manual install is "download the repo as a
# zip, upload it, create the app in the UI", and no distribution route can ship a file that is not in the
# repo — so the local-mode default lives there, committed.
# ⛔ The DAB predeploy (bootstrap/write_app_yaml.py) OVERWRITES it per target with real values, including the
#    deployment's OPERATOR_PASSWORD. After a bundle deploy the tree is dirty: `git checkout app/app.yaml`
#    rather than committing it. The suite has a guard that catches it either way, and it is a stronger one
#    than this ignore line was — an ignore prevents an accident silently, and a test NAMES it.

